Z||000013||StuGood||03-09-2001||10:52 AM||||"Big D," to me, means Dallas!  Regional thing, I guess...<P>Based on very limited impressions, for the most part, I wouldn't want to live in Dallas.  I liked Austin for the most part.  I have friends living in both places, and they are the best features of those cities, of course  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">.  Worst feature of Texas cities?  Too hot, too humid, for too long...<P>Detroit?  Naw, too: ("big city", 'spensive, taxed).  However, I like the region and the people, probably because I'm from northern Indiana.<P>Wichita?  Despite its "too much: (hot+humid+tornados+cold+wind)" syndrome, it's home to me, and some of the nicest, friendliest, most honest people I know live there.  Of course, I've lived there 16 years, off and on.<P>Everett is nice, too, although I'm more familiar with the south Seattle area, and West Seattle.  Too bad it's a little crowded, and housing is so expensive.  Give me about a year, and Everett will feel like home, too  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">     ||||reg||5
